From 28fb0490b2aa1b1cb1dac0ffa52ebff697a5af8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ashforde=20O=C3=9C?= <ashfordegithub@cbaweja.org>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:54:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Kshana Station (L3): the headless receiver service

kshana station run|check|service <station.toml>. Every configured receiver stream (TCP,
serial or USB device, file) is read as it arrives into kshana.obs/1 files through the live
reader obs live uses, so a connection's epochs are a replay's, bit for bit. Files rotate by
size, each starting with the source's header; old files are pruned. A stream that ends is
opened again every second, the gap counted and never filled. A local status port
(GET /health, GET /status; another address needs a bearer token) and an optional fleet
report over HTTP. service prints a systemd unit, a launchd property list or a Windows
start-up task. Read only: nothing is written to a receiver.

Tests over real sockets: a recorded NMEA log served twice (reconnection, files equal to the
replay, obs check on every file), rotation and pruning, the token-guarded status port, the
fleet report with its bearer token, service files and configuration errors. Messages in
the catalogue; machine text in the allowances with reasons.
